#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283246 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Slope-Intercept Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48876e20-f769-587d-899b-e540c2004f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-7y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48876e20-f769-587d-899b-e540c2004f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-7y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283248} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5705ca9-05be-5a28-b721-a34551083b33" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e5a2374-c8a0-52ba-8347-79e5368d0c7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-281236" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x+1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=15.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x+1$ passes through the points $A(0,1)$ and $B(3,2)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 16 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(2,-1)$ and ${B}^{′}(16,7).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+1 & =\\frac{7-(-1)}{16-2}(x-2) \\\\ y+1 & =\\frac{8}{14}(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =\\frac{4}{7}(x-2) \\\\ 7y+7 & =4x-8 \\\\ 4x-7y & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283249 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9038b770-629c-59e3-846f-cd94357fe89e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283251} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe94949-ee3d-5dc9-ac5e-b63612d0d720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9038b770-629c-59e3-846f-cd94357fe89e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283251} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa02b0c-8b31-5c64-9b56-9d19ff5fb2b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2bac187-b724-5e7f-a90f-46647a5ab6f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-281580" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=-1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-8.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=-1$ passes through the points $P(0,-1)$ and $Q(1,-1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(0,2)$ and ${Q}^{′}(4,3).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{3-2}{4-0}(x-0) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{1}{4}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-8 & =x \\\\ x-4y & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7ecfd39-e370-531a-8df6-b1dd1a69f8a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151081} {:answer/id #uuid "a9c25a32-54c5-5d1d-9df2-a505ec1cbbd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151082} {:answer/id #uuid "e467413e-d47c-5654-a000-6679ea89c99c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x - y + 10 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151083} {:answer/id #uuid "30138920-1318-5f1a-8306-6ef024ae6e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - y + 5 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151084} {:answer/id #uuid "75be63f8-653e-5a3c-8fb2-00b29ff3950d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - 5y + 1 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30138920-1318-5f1a-8306-6ef024ae6e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - y + 5 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151084} :answer-field/id #uuid "3caa19ff-ec15-5db3-8fdf-a701ec0cf711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d73144ad-ba24-5f26-a684-3b73d6271ce0" :question/math-academy-id "q-77680" :question/problem "Consider the line $x=5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $x=5$ passes through the points $A(5,0)$ and $B(5,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(-5,0)$ and ${B}^{′}(-4,1).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{1-0}{-4-(-5)}(x-(-5)) \\\\ y & =x+5 \\\\ x-y+5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
